       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long (30 to 50 hours), so the effects would also last a long time. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nCould you check whether one of these applies?\n- **Dosing error:** You may have meant 5 mg once daily, which is the usual starting dose. The range is 2.5 to 10 mg.\n- **Wrong drug or unit:** The order may be meant for a different medication, or the dose may be in the wrong units.\n- **Intentional dose:** If you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, but it would need prescriber confirmation and probably a pharmacy review.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
